WQ-03: track FIFO/LIFO tank volume in the quality solver for overflow

tankmix3() (FIFO) and tankmix4() (LIFO) decide that a tank overflows
when tank->V >= Vmax, but tank->V belongs to the hydraulic solver. After
EN_solveH it holds the volume at the end of the run, so a tank that ends
full books every filling step as overflow. When hydraulics and quality
are stepped together it holds the volume at the end of the step, so the
step that fills a tank is booked as overflow, even for a tank that
cannot overflow. Track each tank's volume in the quality solver (Vq,
from V0 plus each step's net inflow), and treat only the part of the net
inflow that would take Vq above Vmax as overflow, for tanks that can
overflow.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply WQ-03_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/quality.c b/src/quality.c
